      "title": "Mirror Time",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    vector<string> v;\n\n    map<char,char> m{\n        {'0','0'},\n        {'1','1'},\n        {'2','5'},\n        {'5','2'},\n        {'8','8'}\n    };\n\n    for (int h = 0; h < 24; h++) {\n        for (int mi = 0; mi < 60; mi++) {\n            char a = h / 10 + '0';\n            char b = h % 10 + '0';\n            char c = mi / 10 + '0';\n            char d = mi % 10 + '0';\n\n            if (!m.count(a) || !m.count(b) || !m.count(c) || !m.count(d))\n                continue;\n\n            int mh = (m[d] - '0') * 10 + (m[c] - '0');\n            int mm = (m[b] - '0') * 10 + (m[a] - '0');\n\n            if (mh < 24 && mm < 60) {\n                char buf[6];\n                sprintf(buf, \"%02d:%02d\", h, mi);\n                v.push_back(buf);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    string ans = v[0];\n\n    for (auto &t : v)\n        if (t <= s)\n            ans = t;\n\n    cout << ans;\n}",
      "statement": "A digital clock displays time in the format [[HH]]{{:}}[[MM]].\nSome digits remain valid when mirrored, while others become invalid.\nFind the largest valid time less than or equal to the given [[time]] such that its mirrored time is valid.\nValid digit mappings are:\n{{0}} → {{0}}\n{{1}} → {{1}}\n{{2}} → {{5}}\n{{5}} → {{2}}\n{{8}} → {{8}}\nAll other digits are invalid.\nTo compute the mirrored time:\n\nReverse the order of the digits.\nReplace each digit using the mapping above.",
